---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FAQList from '../components/FAQList.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Custom Group Trip Planning',href:'/custom-group-trip-planning/'}];
const faqs=[
  {q:'How custom can the itinerary be?',a:'The planning can begin from the group and trip objective rather than a fixed package. The final degree of customization depends on supplier availability, destination rules, schedule, budget, and group size.'},
  {q:'Can you start from a trip another company already quoted?',a:'Yes. We can review the objectives and structure you are considering, but we will build our own recommendations and supplier approach rather than simply copying another provider’s protected itinerary.'},
  {q:'Can the group choose between several destination options?',a:'Yes. Early planning can compare two or three realistic destinations against the same criteria so the organizer can make a more informed choice.'},
  {q:'Can a custom trip become a repeatable annual program?',a:'Yes. Once a community understands its preferred trip style and traveler profile, later departures can often be developed more efficiently while still improving the itinerary.'}
];
const schema={'@type':'Service',name:'Custom Group Trip Planning',description:'Custom group trip planning for clubs, communities, businesses, studios, teams, friends, and organizer-led departures.',provider:{'@id':`${Astro.site}#organization`},areaServed:{'@type':'Place',name:'Worldwide'}};
const faqSchema={'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faqs.map((i)=>({'@type':'Question',name:i.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:i.a}}))};
---
<BaseLayout title="Custom Group Trip Planning | Talon Expeditions" description="Custom group trip planning for clubs, communities, businesses, studios, teams, friends, and organizer-led departures, with itinerary design and worldwide travel coordination." image={images.planning} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} schema={[schema,faqSchema]}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.planning}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Custom group trip planning</p><h1 class="section-title">Start with the experience you want to create, then build the travel around it.</h1><p>Custom planning is for groups that do not want to select a generic package and hope it fits. Talon Expeditions helps shape the destination, pace, travel structure, support, and participant experience around the real group.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell definition-grid"><div class="definition-sticky"><p class="eyebrow">Plain-language definition</p><h2>What is custom group trip planning?</h2></div><div class="definition-body"><div class="answer-panel"><p>Custom group trip planning means the itinerary and operating structure are developed around a specific group’s goals, dates, likely size, activity level, comfort, and budget rather than requiring the group to join a pre-designed departure. It can include trip design, supplier research, accommodation, transport, activities, organizer support, traveler preparation, and on-trip coordination.</p></div><p>Customization is most useful when the group has a reason for traveling together. A hiking club may want a particular route style. A dive community may need operator capacity and mixed certification options. A business team may want shared activities without a conference schedule. A social group may care most about private time, food, neighborhoods, and cultural experiences.</p><p>Those differences should change the trip. Custom planning gives us room to make those tradeoffs deliberately instead of hiding them behind a standard package name.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Common planning starting points</p><h2 class="section-title">Three common starting points.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">These are not rigid products or pricing tiers. They describe the level of definition a group may have when planning begins.</p></div><div class="package-grid"><div class="package-card"><span class="package-label">Start 01</span><h3>We know the destination</h3><p>The group already has a place, event, route, cruise, or region in mind and needs help turning it into a complete trip.</p><ul><li>Itinerary development</li><li>Supplier and lodging research</li><li>Travel coordination</li><li>Group and readiness planning</li></ul><a class="text-arrow" href="/plan-a-trip/">Start with the destination →</a></div><div class="package-card featured"><span class="package-label">Start 02</span><h3>We know the experience</h3><p>The group knows what it wants to do, learn, or experience, but the destination is still open.</p><ul><li>Destination comparison</li><li>Season and activity fit</li><li>Group-size modeling</li><li>Full itinerary and support design</li></ul><a class="button button-small" href="/plan-a-trip/">Shape the Trip</a></div><div class="package-card"><span class="package-label">Start 03</span><h3>We know the group</h3><p>The organizer has a community and wants to create a trip that fits its interests, budget, and ability.</p><ul><li>Audience and trip-fit discovery</li><li>Concept development</li><li>Viability testing</li><li>Launch and organizer support</li></ul><a class="text-arrow" href="/group-travel/">Explore group formats →</a></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell process-donor"><div class="process-visual" style={`background-image:url('${images.train}')`}><div class="process-callout"><h3>Decisions in the right order.</h3><p>The earlier the trip is, the cheaper and easier it is to change a bad assumption.</p></div></div><div><p class="eyebrow">The planning sequence</p><h2 class="section-title">From broad idea to operational itinerary.</h2><p class="section-copy">We progressively reduce uncertainty. The objective is to avoid committing the group to expensive details before the basic model is viable.</p><div class="process-list"><div class="process-item"><b>Discovery</b><p>Purpose, travelers, dates, source markets, activity, comfort, approximate budget, and organizer priorities.</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Concept</b><p>Destination options, trip style, likely duration, support model, and practical group-size assumptions.</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Design</b><p>Route, lodging, transport, activities, local suppliers, free time, contingency, and commercial structure.</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Launch & prepare</b><p>Participant information, decisions, payments, rooming, documentation, equipment, and final travel coordination.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="feature-band" style={`background-image:url('${images.road}')`}><div class="shell"><div class="band-copy"><p class="eyebrow">A custom trip still needs boundaries</p><h2 class="section-title">Good customization is disciplined, not endless.</h2><p>Every change affects something else. More destinations increase transfers. More optionality may require more vehicles or guides. A lower price may mean fewer private services. A higher activity level may reduce the number of people who can realistically join. We make those tradeoffs visible so customization improves the trip rather than making it incoherent.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p><h2 class="section-title">Before we start designing.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Custom does not mean every component is unlimited or changeable forever. Supplier terms and availability become more important as the trip moves toward confirmation.</p></div><FAQList items={faqs} openFirst={true}/></div></section>
  <PlanningCTA title="Bring us the group, the destination, or the reason to go." />
</BaseLayout>
